<DocsExample TExample="DebugConsoleWriteExample" Title="Record app and user messages" Description="Inject INTDebugConsole and call Write to record what the user did, so the console shows the steps that led to a bug. The console at the bottom of this page is the one these examples write to." />
<DocsExample TExample="DebugConsoleLoggingExample" Title="Capture ILogger output" Description="Everything the session logs through ILogger appears in the console with its level, category and exception. Expand the console, drag its handle to resize it, then scroll up while logging to see it keep your place." />
<DocsExample TExample="DebugConsoleToastExample" Title="Mirror toasts and snackbars" Description="Toasts and snackbars shown through the NT services are added to the console, so it records the feedback the user saw." />
<DocsExample TExample="DebugConsoleSetupExample" Title="Register and place the console" Description="Register the console, place it once in the layout, and pad the page so content is not hidden behind it. On Blazor Server, each circuit's console shows only that circuit's logs, and Authorize decides who may see them." />
